==============================================================================
ORIGINAL WORKS & ATTRIBUTION
==============================================================================

Original assembly routines, mathematical optimizations, and architectural
implementations authored by Shiv Kokroo:
- Target 5 (Xtensa LX7: ESP32-S2 / ESP32-S3): Hand-written unrolled Montgomery
  multiplication (nistp_mul_mont_8, nistp_mul_mont_12), Solinas Montgomery squaring
  (nistp_sqr_mont_8, nistp_sqr_mont_12), and constant-time modular addition/subtraction
  utilizing branchless SALTU carry emulation (Windowed ABI and Call0 ABI).
- Target 1 (ARMv7E-M / ARMv8-M: Cortex-M4 / Cortex-M7 / Cortex-M33): Hand-written
  12-limb unrolled UMAAL Montgomery multiplication (nistp_mul_mont_12), squaring, and
  modular addition/subtraction for NIST P-384 with VFP register allocation.
- Code generation tools (gen/gen_asm_xtensa.py, gen/gen_asm_cortex_m4.py).
- Fast projective/Jacobian ECDSA verification (r * Z^2 == X mod p) eliminating
  expensive field inversions modulo p.
- Interleaved simultaneous double-scalar multiplication (PointJacobian::lincomb /
  Shamir's trick) halving point doublings for P-256 and P-384.
- Fixed-base Comb multiplication tables and Montgomery affine batch inversion.
- Target 2 (ARMv6-M) secp256k1 Comba arithmetic engine and RSA CIOS Montgomery engine.
- Unified multi-target runtime dispatch layer and Embassy crypto driver framework.

